ation, Llama Stack management is available without any opt-in\n- On non-entitled clusters, Llama Stack management is not surfaced\n- No opt-in gate remains\n\nE006:\n\n# Llama Stack GA Documentation Uplift\n\n## Description\nUplift Llama Stack documentation to GA standards, including migration notes from Tech Preview.\n\n## Scope (with content outline inside)\n- GA-standard docs: install/config/supported matrix references, API stability & deprecation policy docs, upgrade/migration guide from TP, guardrails integration guide usage, dashboard default availability\n- Migration notes from TP\n- Technically reviewed against implementation\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- Docs meet GA standards...\n- Migration notes from TP releases present covering the tested upgrade path\n- Technically reviewed against the implemented behavior (Rule 24)\n\nNow frontmatter sets. Then signal files. Then decomposition summary, batch-read, validator, decompose_complete.\n\nOrder per prompt: summary first (8a), then epic files (8b), then verify (8c), final action decompose_complete.\n\nLet me write the summary body now.\n\nSummary sections: Epic List, Dependency DAG (mermaid), DAG Justification, HLR Traceability Matrix, Health Warnings, Tiered Delivery.\n\nAlso include notes on component mappings and missing sections.\n\nNow — team values. \"RHOAI GenAI\", \"TrustyAI\", \"RHOAI Dashboard\", docs epic team \"RHOAI GenAI\"? Hmm, for the Documentation component, maybe there's a docs team. No data. Use \"RHOAI GenAI\" and log the assumption.\n\nLet me write all the files. I'll use Write for bodies (no frontmatter), then frontmatter.py set.\n\nDecomposition summary body:\n\n# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-9014 — Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n...\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n## HLR Traceability Matrix\n\n| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) | Notes |\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable...\n