{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-79677ef0-0053-4e71-95ab-e16f43e9d134","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-90d9b3b281742ff3","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9014-p1ykl22r/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9014-decomposition.md","content":"# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-9014 — Graduate Llama Stack to General Availability\n\nStrategy status: Refinement Done, priority Critical. Llama Stack is Tech\nPreview today (corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.0/llama-stack.md`);\nthe strategy graduates it to GA by closing quality gaps, committing to API\nstability, establishing a production support posture, and promoting the\nTrustyAI guardrails integration and Dashboard default availability.\n\nNo Staff Engineer Input section is present in the strategy.\n\n## Epic List\n\n| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n| E001 | Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment | Investigation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n| E002 | Llama Stack API stability guarantee | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n| E003 | Llama Stack production support posture | Implementation | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n| E004 | TrustyAI guardrails as supported Llama Stack integration | Implementation | TrustyAI | P1 |\n| E005 | Dashboard Llama Stack management enabled by default | Implementation | RHOAI Dashboard | P1 |\n| E006 | Llama Stack GA documentation uplift | Implementation (docs-authoring) | RHOAI GenAI | P0 |\n\nNotes on the epic list:\n\n- **Teams** are taken from the architecture context owning teams (RHOAI GenAI\n  for Llama Stack, TrustyAI for TrustyAI, RHOAI Dashboard for Dashboard). The\n  strategy itself has no Impacted Teams table (see Health Warnings).\n- **E006 component** is the canonical `Documentation` component (from\n  `.context/rhai-components.txt`); its subject matter is Llama Stack GA\n  documentation. E006's team is assumed to be the component owner (RHOAI\n  GenAI) since the strategy names no docs team — flagged in Health Warnings.\n- **E006 priority** is P0 via the docs-authoring priority exception (strategy\n  frontmatter `priority: Critical` → P0), even though HLR-6 is P2 — flagged in\n  Health Warnings.\n\n## Dependency DAG\n\n```mermaid\ngraph TD\n    E001[\"E001 GA-readiness assessment (Investigation, P0)\"]\n    E002[\"E002 API stability guarantee (P0)\"]\n    E003[\"E003 Production support posture (P0)\"]\n    E004[\"E004 TrustyAI guardrails integration (P1)\"]\n    E005[\"E005 Dashboard default enablement (P1)\"]\n    E006[\"E006 GA documentation uplift (docs-authoring, P0)\"]\n    E001 --> E002\n    E001 --> E003\n    E001 --> E004\n    E002 --> E006\n    E003 --> E006\n    E004 --> E006\n    E005 --> E006\n```\n\nCritical path: E001 → E002 → E006 (length 3).\n\n## DAG Justification\n\n| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n|------|------|-----------|\n| E001 → E002 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The GA-readiness assessment produces the definitive GA scope; the size and content of the API stability work is an estimate until it lands (strategy Open Question 1). Gate impact: `rewrite`. |\n| E001 → E003 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The supported configuration matrix and SLO targets are sized by the assessment's scale-limit and error-handling findings. Gate impact: `rewrite`. |\n| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates downstream) | The assessment inventories gaps against the GA bar for the whole distribution; it may reveal additional guardrails-integration hardening beyond the known experimental-flag gap. Gate impact: `add_remediation` — the base integration work is defined by HLR-4 regardless. |\n| E002 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs last) | GA documentation must describe the published API versioning, deprecation policy, and tested upgrade path once built. |\n| E003 → E006 | Rule 11 (docs last) | GA documentation references the published