ility guarantee: versioned APIs, deprecation policy, tested upgrade path from last two TP releases | E002 | Direct mapping. |\n| HLR-3 | P0 | Production support posture: documented SLO targets, backport policy, supported configuration matrix | E003 | Direct mapping. Kept separate from E002: different logical change and work-product type (support-process definition vs. API hardening). |\n| HLR-4 | P1 | TrustyAI guardrails a supported, documented integration for GA distributions | E004 | Direct mapping; passive side (Llama Stack distribution accepting the integration) is captured as an acceptance criterion on E004 verifying against a GA distribution configuration. |\n| HLR-5 | P1 | Dashboard enables Llama Stack management by default for entitled clusters | E005 | Direct mapping. |\n| HLR-6 | P2 | Documentation uplifted to GA standards, including TP migration notes | E006 | Direct mapping; docs-authoring epic blocked by all Implementation epics per Rule 11. Priority P0 via docs-authoring exception (strategy priority Critical). |\n\nAll six HLRs are covered; none is bundled — each maps to exactly one epic.\n\n## Health Warnings\n\n1. **Missing strategy sections** (non-blocking): the strategy has no Impacted\n   Teams table, no Dependencies table, no formal Given/When/Then acceptance\n   criteria, and no Non-Functional Requirements section. Teams were derived\n   from architecture context; epic acceptance criteria were derived from the\n   HLRs and strategy problem statement.\n2. **Docs epic priority divergence**: HLR-6 is P2, but the docs-authoring\n   priority exception derives E006's priority from the strategy-level\n   `priority: Critical` → P0. This is per-rule but diverges from the HLR's own\n   priority; humans should confirm the docs uplift is actually scheduled at\n   P0 urgency.\n3. **Docs epic team assumption**: the strategy names no owning team for the\n   documentation uplift. E006 is assigned to RHOAI GenAI (the Llama Stack\n   owner); if a dedicated docs team owns GA content, reassign before\n   submission.\n4. **Release sequencing vs. build dependency for E005**: the Dashboard\n   default-on flip has no DAG edge to the Llama Stack GA epics because it is\n   build-independent, but shipping default-on before Llama Stack actually\n   graduates would contradict the strategy's intent. Coordinate the release:\n   default-on should land with (not before) the GA graduation.\n5. **Scope trap watch (HLR-3)**: \"documented SLO targets\" implies measurement.\n   If establishing the SLOs turns out to require new observability/telemetry\n   infrastructure in Llama Stack, that is net-new engineering beyond\n   documenting targets and should be re-scoped when the E001 assessment lands.\n6. **Estimate uncertainty (strategy Open Question 1)**: until E001 lands, the\n   size of E002/E003/E004 is an estimate — this is exactly why all three are\n   gated on E001 rather than split further now. Premature splitting on an\n   unvalidated estimate would produce artificial boundaries.\n\n## Tiered Delivery\n\nNot applicable — no external dependency with uncertain timing (no upstream\nPR/RFC or vendor coordination gates this strategy). The parallel structure is:\nE005 (Dashboard default enablement) is fully independent Tier-1-style work\nthat can proceed immediately; E002/E003/E004 are gated on the E001 assessment\nresolving the GA scope; E006 (docs) is last by rule.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":29873,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-bac38a08cb6af61f","agent_id":"a128e164fc4701093","session_id":"44c1731f-e230-44d3-a6db-ee0916001d72","uuid":"d69b23c6-00d2-4d32-b63d-2d9f6d5fe169","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:14:07.886Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9014 into epics"}
