{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b00547ff22181ba9","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# AI Signals Rationale: RHAISTRAT-9014-E001 — Llama Stack GA-readiness assessment\n2\t\n3\tInvestigation epic — scored with the 5 investigation signals.\n4\t\n5\t| Signal | Value | Rationale |\n6\t|--------|-------|-----------|\n7\t| question_specificity | +1 | The strategy enumerates the GA-bar dimensions to assess (API stability, upgrade paths, scale limits, error handling) and defines the deliverable (gap inventory + definitive GA scope). Pass/fail criterion is well defined: an inventory covering each dimension with current state, GA bar, and severity, plus an accepted scope document. |\n8\t| source_accessibility | +1 | Readable artifacts exist that contain or determine the answer: the midstream repo (opendatahub-io/llama-stack-k8s-operator), upstream meta-llama/llama-stack, the architecture context file, and internal support tickets holding the scattered TP feedback. Nothing depends on a decision still under review. |\n9\t| local_runnability | 0 | The platform component is a Kubernetes operator managing LlamaStackDistribution CRs; exercising the distribution end to end (and its error behavior) realistically requires a cluster rather than a standalone binary/pip library, so the desk-research parts are local but the component is not trivially runnable locally. |\n10\t| cluster_hardware_dependence | -1 | The gating question (gap inventory against the four named dimensions) is answerable from source, tickets, and docs; peripheral questions — scale limits and error handling under load — need a live cluster to measure, so some but not the gating questions are cluster-dependent. |\n11\t| human_judgment_required | -1 | The technical inventory is resolvable without stakeholders, but the final GA scope (what is in vs. out of the GA bar) is a product/support commitment that requires stakeholder acceptance — a peripheral human decision on top of the technical findings, not the gating question itself. |\n12\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83248e61379c6dd8","agent_id":"a60b08dd582e62c70","session_id":"44c1731f-e230-44d3-a6db-ee0916001d72","uuid":"bf0fe0a3-31d5-44ce-9449-fe594b29b7be","timestamp":"2026-10-26T13:17:14.982Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b00547ff22181ba9","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9014 decomposition"}
